-- title:
--   Left Tensor Pair Prefix Adjoint Normalization
-- statement:
--   **Adjoint left-tensor prefixes are normalized.** For finite submeasurements `A` and `B`, let `E_b = leftTensor (A.total * B.outcome b)`. The adjoint ordering of the same family also has total mass bounded by the identity.
--
--   $$
--   \sum_{b : β} E_b^{\dagger} E_b \le I_{ι \times ι}.
--   $$
--
--   The result is the adjoint normalization side condition needed by the final reverse estimate `evaluatedSlice_phaseNine_tail_bound`.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Commutativity.leftTensor_pair_prefix_adjoint_normalization`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
